config BR2_PACKAGE_WEBVIEW
	bool "webview"
	depends on BR2_PACKAGE_WPEWEBKIT
	select BR2_PACKAGE_LIBXKBCOMMON
	select BR2_PACKAGE_XKEYBOARD_CONFIG # runtime, keymaps
	help
	  Full-screen web surface for openHC.

	  Creates one WPE WebKit view, loads a URL and runs a main loop. No
	  chrome, no navigation, no tabs -- the display path lives entirely in
	  the libwpe backend, so this is only the part WPE does not ship
	  (Buildroot builds WebKit with ENABLE_MINIBROWSER=OFF).

	  The URL comes from argv[1] or $WEBVIEW_URL, defaulting to
	  http://localhost/ -- the dashboard webd already serves on :80.
	  What any other URL serves is not openHC's concern.

	  USB keyboards and mice drive the page: through libinput on WPE
	  Platform's DRM display, and on the libwpe path by reading
	  /dev/input directly (keymaps from xkeyboard-config). The page
	  draws the mouse cursor itself.

comment "webview needs wpewebkit"
	depends on !BR2_PACKAGE_WPEWEBKIT
